Still 1.2.0. Pocket mode, and the tap detector rebuilt around a measurement.

Settings keeps one switch. A green slider at the bottom arms it: the screen locks and the microphone closes. Three taps on the phone within three seconds open it, three more close it. The red slider unlocks.

Frequency turned out not to tell a tap from music, whatever the band — attack does. Real music went from 52 false triggers an hour to none, and your phone-tap recording now scores ten of ten.
